OAKLAND TECH DIGEST
Friday, August 28, 2026

Hi neighbors,

Summer is winding down and the calendar is filling back up. Here is what is happening in East Bay tech over the next two weeks.

THIS WEEK
- Fifth Street Foundry, the makerspace on Fifth near Broadway, is taking over the adjacent warehouse bay and adding a second CNC router and a paint booth. The membership waitlist reopens September 8.
- The city's small-business office extended the storefront-activation grant deadline to September 30; tech companies taking ground-floor space downtown qualify.

COMING UP
- Tue Sep 1, 6:00pm | Uptown Hardware Meetup at Fifth Street Foundry. Two lightning talks (a low-cost vibration-sensor build; a teardown of a 1990s PLC) and open shop time. Free. RSVP: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/hw-sep1
- Thu Sep 3, 8:00am | Founders Coffee, Temescal. No agenda, no pitches, just coffee at the Alcatraz Avenue place with the big table. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/coffee-sep3
- Thu Sep 10, 6:30pm | East Bay Robotics Demo Night, Jack London Square. Six teams, five minutes each, a working robot required. Applications for a demo slot close Sep 4. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/robots-sep10

COMMUNITY
- The Oakland Public Library's main branch is starting a weekly "AI for small business" drop-in on Tuesday afternoons through October.
- A reader is organizing a group drive to the Sacramento hardware expo in October; reply to this email if you want a seat.

JOBS BOARD
- Controls engineer, Alameda (small automation integrator)
- Community manager, Fifth Street Foundry
- Firmware engineer, a Jack London Square startup (they asked us not to name them yet)
Post a job: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/jobs

See you around the lake,
Desmond

